ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_10 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_11 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Introduction (ghost chapter)"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9c3488421d2316a734c6d2ace7a96153"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "the Perfectly Self-Enlightened One"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1004 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1005,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1006,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_176,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_441 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "THINKING PROCESSES"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "4de3b38e64a8dc7bb55428876e55e40f"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "If you can see the wanting to think, know that. Observe the intensity of the wanting. When, through skillful observation, the wanting diminishes, the thoughts will also diminish. If you can't see the intentions to think just switch back and forth between thoughts and body as objects."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1007 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1008,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_290,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_555,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_817 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "LOST IN THOUGHT"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "052b28cdb9d96f4598aa552f85441313"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Do you know that you are walking when you are walking around in daily life? You will often be lost in thought. If you realize that this is happening, just know, \"The mind is thinking.\" What is important is what is happening in this moment. You can do what you need to do when you arrive at your destination; there's no need to think about it now. This way the mind will also think less about the future. You can expend a lot of mental energy speculating about the future without actually knowing what is going to happen. If you discover a very different outcome than what you had expected, you have spent a lot of energy on imagination!"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1009 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1010,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1011 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "LOST IN THOUGHT"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "b4773dc6199bc1f30bd1ad08a478cccb"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "There was a businessman who went to the market to buy goods wholesale to resell later. His journey to the market was filled with thoughts of various prices, how he would try to get there before everybody to get the first pick of goods. When he arrived he found there was nothing there for him! This businessman was a yogi and so he was aware of what his mind was doing this whole time. He realized how much time he had wasted speculating and determined that on future market trips he would relax and make decisions when he arrived."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1012 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1013,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1014,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_171,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_267,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_366,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_434,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_82 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MEMORIES AND PLANNING"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "7dc4c1c322fa2b4dda1268228318a4d9"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "The concept or story is about the past or future but the knowing of that is in the present moment. You need to consider how you might respond to a certain situation so that you arrive prepared, but this is not the same as worrying about a situation. If you are planning and knowing with wisdom that this is happening, that's the present moment. Planning is necessary but could be done with either defilements or wisdom. Do you worry when you're planning? Some people plan with greed and others with anxiety but there is a way to plan and think in a relaxed way."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1015 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1016,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1017,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_139,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_847 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MEMORIES AND PLANNING"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "6bf195a69c1050490c5883329e861d4b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Thinking about past events will also happen naturally from time to time and there's nothing you can do about it. You can't go back and change the situation. You can only revisit the past in thought. However, you can learn a lesson and not repeat the same mistakes. One yogi realized that the idea of \"one second\" of time was a concept and the past dropped away for him with this understanding."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1018 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1019,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1020,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1021,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_16,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_33 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "AWARENESS AT WORK"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e8a90349cd10d1230599e256c881d830"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "Meditating at work is a skill and by skill, I mean lots of practice! Initially, of course, when you pay attention to outside phenomena, you can't concentrate on phenomena inside; when you put your mind inside you can't really be aware of what is happening outside. Initially you might not be able to be aware of inside and outside when you are working but try to practice whenever you can to allow momentum to build. At some point awareness will kick in naturally while you're doing something you're really absorbed in. Getting to this level of awareness requires consistent practice."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1022 a neo:__Entity__ ;
    neo:INVOLVES ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1021 ;
    neo:id "Medit,Ating At Work"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:llm_model_name "qwen3:8b"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1023 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1024,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_16,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_290 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "AWARENESS AT WORK"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "907c83a998912439e2462ee6bd182fae"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "When you need to be working, just do it fully. Sometimes you will have more time to devote to your practice and do it freely and you will know something like, \"Oh the mind is thinking about this so it can do that.\" When you build the habit of noticing the mind at work then you will notice that awareness just starts popping up because it becomes a habit for the mind to recognize itself doing work. This will just come in naturally. Allow this to happen."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1025 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1026,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1027,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1028,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_139,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_323 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "AWARENESS AT WORK"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "de2e28d083eb939ad1a2bcf8c451795b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "A yogi once asked a question about building up continuous practice, \"How much should we do?\" I said, \"Do it 50-50.\" The yogi was a psychiatrist so he thought a moment about my suggestion and asked, \"How do you measure?\" (Laughter.) I considered it and realized that it wasn't as much about a division of 50-50 as much as allowing the mind to do its work naturally. If it is very practiced then the knowing happens naturally."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1030 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1026,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1031,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1032,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_162,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_290,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_620 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "AWARENESS AT WORK"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "2ec992ed3d5207a4df71b43c153b6f4c"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "When you have a continuous practice that reminds and remembers and knows the mind at work, then it gets to the point where it becomes effortless because the mind becomes so familiar and so intimate with itself. It is always with itself and it likes being with itself. That's when it allows the mind to do anything because it doesn't mind; it's always with itself. The operative word is continuously. Although it is difficult in the beginning, any amount of effort you put in brings momentum and that in turn makes it more effortless and continuous in the future. That's why the Buddha said to practice continuously. WHEN THE MIND SAYS, \"IT'S NOT FAIR .\" When something happens, the mind starts making judgments, sets up parameters, and develops ideas of what's appropriate and boundaries of \"you\" and \"me.\" Once hooked on these ideas, the mind won't like it when one of these ideas is violated."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1033 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1034,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1035,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1036,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1037,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1038,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_295,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_497 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "AWARENESS AT WORK"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "35c00e852fd122613fa9c0b6b3fd7f58"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "We encounter this all the time. In Western society, people wait in a queue or line because there is a belief that people should wait their turn for something. There is a dissonance when someone cuts that queue/line and thoughts that they should be in line start coming up. Or different thoughts of fairness might come up. There could be another kind of belief, \"I wanted to get to my food and she has slowed that down by jumping the queue.\" The mind has convinced itself of all these strands of thought! At times like these, we should ask ourselves, \"What internal belief is being thwarted here?\" Right now, someone's actions are frustrating these beliefs and the mind justifies this anger against the other person!"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1039 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1040,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1041,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1042,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1043,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1044,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_176,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_468,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_509 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "STRINGING EACH OTHER ALONG"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "f04e3ba8e56411e146a944a0dec7a39b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "In daily life, we give each other compliments and thank each other for their compliments. We string each other along by reinforcing the need to look good and feel good. If instead we had said, \"You look really terrible,\" the listener might get irritated because people want to feel good. We are often at the mercy of other people's words, compliments or insults and are generally automatically affected. When there is an understanding of how these thoughts work in the background, the wanting will disappear."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1046 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1047,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1048,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1049,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1050,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1051,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1052,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1053,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1054,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1055,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_28,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_352 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "FEELING LIKE BEING TAKEN ADVANTAGE OF"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "9cd9a28644f164ffd7f6c076453a5b6e"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "It is very important that there is a right attitude when we are working in the world. Sometimes we may feel like we are being taken advantage of or being taken for granted. How different would it be if we thought these people were acting in a certain way because they didn't know any better? If someone were bullying you, it would be really tough to handle! You may get tense, agitated or angry with the bully. What if you thought that this person was only inadvertently doing these things because she didn't know better? How would you feel then? You can better understand and forgive. SELF-JUDGMENTS \"Bad\" is just a label. Don't label yourself that. When the mind is wholesome, the person is good and when the mind is unwholesome, the person is bad. It's only for that moment and that's always changing. Continue to practice and take your time; the fact that you are practicing shows that your mind wants to become better and that means that the mind will become better."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1056 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1057,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1058,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_177,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_290 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "FEELING LIKE BEING TAKEN ADVANTAGE OF"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "b03e7db145de7391c39b00dbcac02b2f"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "When doubt is strong in the mind, do not pay attention to these thoughts. Once we give attention to these kinds of thoughts, they suck us in and grow. We can anchor ourselves to feelings instead and not give any power to the conceptual thinking. Follow the same principle for other strong, unwholesome states. When we look at the feeling and discontinue looking at the thoughts, it will help the mind calm down. Then we can look at these thoughts and feelings together when we feel we're ready."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1059 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1060,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1061,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1062,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1063,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_184,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_290,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_364,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_52 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "FEELING LIKE BEING TAKEN ADVANTAGE OF"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "86c020c903f2a99bf0be76a13ba201f6"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "Everyone has his or her own path and there's a natural course that needs to unfold for each person. You can watch what's happening in the mind and understand it, but you can't force it. You may learn a technique at a retreat, but it is when you go home that you can apply that technique all the time. That's when your life changes."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1064 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1065,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1066,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1067,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1068 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "PRECONCEPTIONS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "261694bb8ac27232b5585ebb73848a52"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "How do you experience silence? How do you experience the stillness of a garden or the woods? I've asked different people this question. Fear comes up for some people. Youngsters tell me that they get bored when there's nothing to occupy them. As you can see, good or bad depends on the person experiencing it, depending on their preconceived feelings of it."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1069 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1070,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1071,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1072,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1073,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_64 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "PRECONCEPTIONS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "436f3e8deeb643754bc31af1f3d13cfe"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "There are tons of these accumulations that you have from childhood and you really want to see these ideas that have built up over the years. If these little preconceptions are seen properly, then the mind will no longer be disturbed by what is happening. If you continue to meditate regularly, there ought to be fewer and fewer attachments."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1075 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1011,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1076,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1077,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_295,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_323,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_932 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "GIVING COMES IN DIFFERENT WAYS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "692445517f6d93256d01857a7f7eab75"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "The market where I had my shop was a very busy place. Lots of shops were lined up side by side with narrow alleys between them. Shopkeepers sent goods in and out with carriers who ran back and forth for the shopkeepers. People would run quite blindly, not caring who was in the way. I would get irritated whenever I had to get out of the way, which was quite often! I knew that people would run into me if I didn't move aside, but also became annoyed that I was the one who always had to be careful. This was a daily occurrence."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1078 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1044,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1079,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1080,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1081,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1082,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1083,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_195,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_224,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_619,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_83 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "GIVING COMES IN DIFFERENT WAYS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "18a8aa1e56fd7f3334d2bdd080b8ee1d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "When I began to practice continuously, I became mindful of my irritation with this market situation. After being mindful of it regularly for a long time, I actually began to see it as a good practice to give space to these people to prevent accidents and I saw moving aside as a practice of generosity. As I practiced day after day and mindfulness arose, good actions also followed. The aversion that accompanied the critical mind decreased. With aversion gone, I began to feel metta for these people."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1084 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1085,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_16,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_171,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_290,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_360,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_777 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "DIFFERENT EXPERIENCES, DIFFERENT REACTIONS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "715f307d8e38bf022192e42fda594003"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "In daily life, where wisdom may be weak, you want initially to pay attention to awareness. The mind can recognize the situation happening while awareness naturally collects data in the background. As awareness picks up more data from the experience, and the picture becomes complete and wholesome minds grow stronger, you will eventually stop acting out of defilements."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1086 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1087,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1088,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1089,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_16,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_171,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_174,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_360,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_65,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_915 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "DIFFERENT EXPERIENCES, DIFFERENT REACTIONS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "72bf6cf8ee3d7c1094e1994eccb0ada9"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "Let's say you are in a social situation and you have accidentally said something harsh because there was too much momentum to speak. Let awareness continue to know in the background while you're talking to others. At some point of seeing this whole process, awareness will have enough of a picture that wisdom can arise and resolve the situation. It is inevitable to make some wrong turns in daily life but you have to learn how to profit from these experiences. Don't allow defilements to run freely or your situation will deteriorate."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1090 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1091,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1092,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_16,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_725,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_84 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "DIFFERENT EXPERIENCES, DIFFERENT REACTIONS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "2356bef32e52c240cd08419a3dcd76f2"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "Imagine the alternate result if only delusion were operating. Perhaps that situation would become exaggerated. We have to recognize things for what they are. If the mind has a bad habit, we have to recognize that. There is awareness so you're keenly aware of what goes through your mind. It takes time and everybody has different characteristics. We all have faults and we need to look at what is in our mind and know it until the mind realizes that it doesn't want to be that way anymore. That realization will help you learn how to let go."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1093 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1094,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1095,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_184,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_387,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_735 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "DIFFERENT EXPERIENCES, DIFFERENT REACTIONS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "983098e55edde46e08173b40251d5cc2"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "We think that there are many people that we interact with in our daily lives. In fact, most of us will usually interact with a certain limited set of people over and over again. How do we work with this? How can we strategize so that we become skillful? So long as there is the intention to have the Dhamma in our lives, then it will become easier."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1096 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1097,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1098,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1099,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1100,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1101,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_184,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_777 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Day-to-Day"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "DIFFERENT EXPERIENCES, DIFFERENT REACTIONS"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c40bc3baeea157cc46b650afc176e723"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "Having these experiences is very important and each experience gives you a life lesson. It's like playing videogames, which I like to talk about with children. You work at it and reach the first level. You graduate to higher and higher levels and eventually win the prize. You know how to do this because you've got that experience. You know how you can win this game at this level. Of course if you don't know how to learn from your experiences, you won't get anything no matter how many life lessons come your way!"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1102 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1103,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1104 ;
