        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_350,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_351,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_352,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_353,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_354,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_355 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "A Note from the Teacher"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "6edd243b7499591bad0b2c6cb3620798"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 30 ;
    neo:text "Finally, we all have to live, but we must ask ourselves: Are we truly alive? If we don't change and grow, it is akin to being dead. I encourage all of you to please continue practicing. I make an aspiration for all of you to practice at home and to enjoy the fruits of your practice."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_356 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_16,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_171,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_290,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_30,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_357,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_358 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "A Note from the Teacher"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ae9f8e0ebb5bdaa867aeb12ecc3b82d4"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 31 ;
    neo:text "When I know the mind is aware, there is a very strong feeling of goodness. I greatly wish for yogis to understand and appreciate fully the value of awareness + wisdom and their role in helping develop all of the wholesome qualities of the mind. This is the basic understanding that will carry the rest of the practice."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_359 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_139,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_360,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_52 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "dcad7165cd01e3c42a5e5eee548d0d27"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "When a retreat begins, defilements will negotiate with the yogi: \"Okay, how long do you want to practice for? One month? Two months? Three months? All right. We'll leave you alone for that long. But when the retreat is over, then it's our turn again!\" And it really is their turn again. Delusion loves hearing the line, \"The retreat is over!\" It is very common to think that we've finished meditating. When this happens, it is now time for defilements to come back out to play."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_36 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_1,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_37,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_38 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Dear Reader"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "acfc4254efb0e976042d9e36b1589e17"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "It doesn't take long for a yogi (meditator) new to Sayadaw U Tejaniya to notice humor permeating his teachings. Whether it is making an observation on his surroundings or commenting on the environment of the mind, Sayadaw, or \"the Teacher\" as his disciples fondly call him, delivers his teachings with a good dose of wit."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_361 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_184,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_215,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_290,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_362,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_363 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "2859dcc8229ec21dacd16a292c416f09"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "When I was younger, I went for long retreats of six to ten months at a time. My mind cleared up while I was in retreat but I stopped practicing back home and my mind went back to square one. My life did not change. I never listened to my teacher's advice to continue practicing at home and got into deep trouble! It was only when I was in the deepest trouble that I saw the need to work it out in daily life. I began to practice continuously at home and realized the need to meditate all the time."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_365 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_195,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_219,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_366 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "52f4b26f892e3939d98e1a93e1eb1b6d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "When you return home, remember that you are there, at home. You should remain in the present moment there. The present moment is the only real thing. Stay where you are because the now is always now, there is no \"after now.\" You're trying to have mindfulness in this mind and the only effort is to remember to be mindful in the present moment. Through everything in your life you are remembering to be mindful, remembering how to be mindful, and building and maintaining samadhi, or stability of the mind."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_367 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_310,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_33,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_368,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_369,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_370,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_371,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_372 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "1dc56b3d85cc9ba986cb58bde502dafd"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "You use the information that you have, combined with intelligence, logic, and reasoning to figure out how to practice correctly. Next, you learn how to keep these already developed insights alive. Finally, you figure out how to develop even deeper levels of insight."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_374 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_219,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_27,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_375,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_376,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_377 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MEDITATING ALL THE TIME"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e16d8ed1b4470f7b207885b02208ffc5"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "We must be walking on the Noble Eightfold Path of sila (moral conduct), samadhi (stability of mind), and panna (wisdom). This particular aspect of meditation, where you need to be practicing it all the time for it to be alive and beneficial becomes apparent to someone who practices continuously. We really need to be a close friend of the Dhamma in order to grow in the Dhamma. It is when we are in such close communion with the Dhamma that we can grow in it. Otherwise, there is not much growth. How can the Dhamma grow in us if we are not always living the Dhamma?"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_379 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_27,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_360,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_380,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_64,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_84 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MEDITATING ALL THE TIME"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "62e110b6e8a592d8c37ad516c7a53772"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "The Buddha frequently reminded his followers to keep the Dhamma in mind. He didn't say when to have the Dhamma in mind, but just said to have the Dhamma in mind. Unless we are always meditating, delusion will step in and hold the door open for all the other defilements to move in."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_381 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_295,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_382,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_383,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_384,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_52,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_64,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_82 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MEDITATING ALL THE TIME"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "aed88926b9a73766b3cb4f9e47761650"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "People talk about how long they have been practicing meditation but they are only counting the length of time from their first retreat up to now. If they added up the hours that they were actually mindful, that would be a wholly different picture. The way we usually work is to put in a lot of effort over a small period of time in the hopes of getting some reward. That's greed at work!"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_385 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_165,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_171,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_386,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_387,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_65 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MEDITATING ALL THE TIME"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "339adba11f35ac1e1471f969d998167a"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "Right effort is staying in it for the long haul. You need to become familiar with the work that you do, to always be in touch with it so that you become skillful at it. Right effort is not letting it slack off, not giving up, and never stopping. Keep going. That's real, right effort. Wisdom considers the long term. There's no hurry but we also do not rest. The more we understand the forces of nature and how they work, the more we begin to rely on the laws of nature to let things unfold in a steady way. It is also not for nothing that I'm using this word nature over and over. When something becomes your nature, really second nature, it means that the momentum of that nature is very strong in you. It has become your nature."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_388 a neo:__Entity__ ;
    neo:LEADS_TO ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_394 ;
    neo:id "Understanding Nature"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:llm_model_name "qwen3:8b"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_395 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_396,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_397,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_398,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_399,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_400,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_65 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MEDITATING ALL THE TIME"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "5ca0b2eb6db2cabcfce2d6a2d5d87621"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "Momentum is important in every sphere of our lives and it is what makes things better and better. When there is momentum, it's not only easier to do what we have to do but also easier to grow our expertise and improve. If you were a high jumper, you would run to gain momentum so you can jump over the hurdle. Right now, you may run towards the hurdle, look up, realize how high it is, stop, turn, and walk back! You didn't have enough momentum to take the jump."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_40 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_27,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_41,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_42,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_43,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_44,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_45 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Dear Reader"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "e26bae4bf09103f9d225bb52324714d3"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "While the delivery may come with a bit of levity, Sayadaw is quite serious about the subject of Dhamma. Using his own experiences as guide and gradually honing his presentation, Sayadaw encourages meditators to always be persistent, experiment, and dig deeper into the Dhamma. He relates to his lay students through pithy business metaphors and regularly describes his own experiences in learning to meditate in the midst of managing the family business and before ordaining permanently in 1996."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_401 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_16,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_169,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_171,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_290,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_323,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_360,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_64 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MEDITATING ALL THE TIME"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "bab2bedfaa2d4e031d811261ab53885b"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 6 ;
    neo:text "I would ask you to look at your mind right now. How often do defilements come in unnoticed? You've got to turn that whole paradigm upside down so that what is natural and unnoticed and always going on in your mind is awareness, stability of mind, and wisdom, just as the defilements are present right now. If you ask me about setting aside time for meditation, yes, we should do that. It is a time, whether we sit or use some other form, that we determine that we will have in mind to be mindful most continuously. When I was at home, I sat before I went to work in the morning and before I went to sleep at night. I also sat from time to time throughout the day in my shop or at the coffee shop. When there was a lull in my work or I had 5 or 10 minutes, I would be still and do meditation. All of these things gathered my mind."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_402 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_195,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_403,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_404,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_405,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_406 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MEDITATING ALL THE TIME"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "658bed910383d31a8ac8926066286f0c"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 7 ;
    neo:text "We haven't reached the point where practicing continuously in daily life feels essential for us, so much so that we cannot live without it. If we felt that way about practice in our daily lives, we would maintain mindfulness so much more continuously. When we want to maintain the peace in our mind for longer and longer periods, we begin to realize that all these elements of knowing what we are aware of must become part of our practice and skill. Otherwise, we cannot maintain the peacefulness of the mind because we lose it when we lose awareness like a leaky faucet loses water. We leak peacefulness when we lose mindfulness while talking, walking or going about our daily business."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_407 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_310,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_33,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_408,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_409,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_410,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_64 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MEDITATING ALL THE TIME"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c570d00bf4f31460dcd98e6aadbc9bdc"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 8 ;
    neo:text "Let's use a business analogy to think about meditation. You secure some initial funding and you need to use your seed capital appropriately to start a business. So far, you have done retreats. Once the cash starts coming in, you learn to maintain that cash flow. In meditation, you now have to consider how to keep insights alive in your daily life. Do you know how to do that? To keep insights from fading, you have to allow these understandings to arise over and over in your mind. Continue practicing at home, as you would on a retreat. Once you can keep your insights alive and developing and keep your practice going, your business is now well established. You can grow it even more. You can dedicate yourself to expanding your business. If you do not, instead of being like entrepreneurs, you may be like day laborers who make just enough money to survive day-to-day."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_411 a neo:__Entity__ ;
    neo:KEEP_ALIVE ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_310 ;
    neo:id "Medit,Ation"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:llm_model_name "qwen3:8b"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_414 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_30,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_323,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_33,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_415,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_416,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_65 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MEDITATING ALL THE TIME"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "f7c50d52ff20c388dada825074a68d2d"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 9 ;
    neo:text "Does all this discourage you or propel you to press forward and go the distance? Sometimes it is hard to tell yogis the truth because I worry that I might make it all sound too difficult! (Laughs.) But it's the truth. Can you imagine how much practice that is going to take? We want to turn the momentum of the current mind completely around so that it is going in the direction of wholesome momentum rather than unwholesome momentum. Now, when we look, it is natural for liking and disliking to arise. When we hear something, liking and disliking arises in the mind. That is natural for us now. Later, with more practice, it becomes natural for awareness + wisdom to be present when we look, hear, smell, touch, taste, or think. Then we can begin to trust that awareness + wisdom."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_417 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_16,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_219,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_224,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_271,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_272,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_33,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_418 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MAINTAINING A STABLE MIND"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "edd43dbc3a92ce89f12b6f628c09cb30"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 1 ;
    neo:text "While I began practicing from a young age, I really started practicing at home in the midst of much suffering. I was in constant pain and sleep was my only rest. Every morning I woke up and the difficulty started again. I did not communicate much at the time. The only question I asked myself at that time was, \"Why is the mind suffering?\" This question really motivated me to keep watching the mind all the time. At first it was just suffering and I didn't know why. But slowly, from watching that continuously, awareness and samadhi grew and the mind became more peaceful. There was less suffering."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_419 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_16,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_195,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_225,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_290,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_420 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MAINTAINING A STABLE MIND"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "2669551c7db04a19d13237f28d14a518"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 2 ;
    neo:text "When the mind began to have more peace then I made peace the main object for my awareness. Peacefulness became the anchor for my mind. Knowing the peaceful mind, I was also aware of everything else that was happening in the mind. I wasn't interested in whatever level of wisdom I had achieved; I understood that if I were mindful, there would be some relief. I knew that whenever I meditated, the depression was reduced a little. I understood that much."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_422 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_16,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_423,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_424 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MAINTAINING A STABLE MIND"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "91da79efbca35e241dc5b1519b85f123"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 3 ;
    neo:text "I kept an eye on the peacefulness and on whether it was being maintained or disturbed with whatever contact there was with external or internal experiences. When you are aware of a peaceful mind, it continues to be peaceful. It becomes more and more peaceful. When you aren't aware of the peaceful mind then the mind starts breaking down into chaos."^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_425 a neo:Document ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MAINTAINING A STABLE MIND"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "ad86f79ef384c06f2e1f4a28b06dfd90"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 4 ;
    neo:text "How long can you maintain stability of mind in daily life?"^^xsd:string .

ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_426 a neo:Document ;
    neo:MENTIONS ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_162,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_171,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_290,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_360,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_427,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_428,
        ex:node_4_037c2398_17b8_4f53_9503_29faec04f111_429 ;
    neo:h1 "COLLECTING GOLD DUST: Nurturing the Dhamma in Daily Living"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h2 "Mindfulness is a Lifestyle Change"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:h3 "MAINTAINING A STABLE MIND"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:id "c54241467de5cafd6f2a4422cc9da471"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_name "2019_-_Sayadaw-U-Tejaniya-Collecting-Gold-Dust-Web-Book-1_-_local_converter.md"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:jejune_source_slug "collecting-gold-dust"^^xsd:string ;
    neo:paragraph_number 5 ;
    neo:text "The Buddha said that when there are leaves covering the surface of a lake, you can't see your reflection. Also when the water is turbulent, you can't see your reflection. It is the same with the mind. Stability and wisdom cannot arise when the mind is covered with defilements."^^xsd:string .

